Here are a few suggestions:

 It's a minor prose nitpick, but excessive prepositional phrases hurt your clarity and conciseness. I have the same problem, and recommend running your writing through Slickwrite.com to catch it.
 is a bit too subjective for my liking. Also, the author can't really know that unless they also tasted it. Maybe say that subjects report the flavor as balanced.
 feels weird. Does that part just cease to exist? It might make more sense to say that it deteriorates
SCP-3178-1 feel really disconnected from the rest of the SCP. I'd either remove them or find a way to more smoothly incorporate them.
Test logs are good, but a couple of them seem a bit repetitive, maybe remove a couple


On the whole, I think the concept definitely has potential, but there are too many issues for me to give it a +1, so I'm going to make it a non-vote.







